 "v1_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to 1180-1260/month in Aug-Sep 2026 (E-07). The dominant driver is a billing-side defect producing wrong bills independent of read source: 59% of disputed bills (1785 of 3025) involve correctly-captured ACTUAL meter reads, not estimate-substituted ones (E-02), ruling out AMI/field-read failures as the main cause; tariff changes are also ruled out (E-04). The best-supported remaining mechanism, uncontradicted in current evidence, is a change to billing import validation rules around August (H-RULE-CHANGE) causing systematic bill errors at the \"billing import + validation\" step, which then surface as dispute tickets at \"bill issue\" / \"dispute ticket\".",
